
Question 11: Select employees whose name is not 'Amit'.
Consider an employee table with the following fields:
id, name, salary, email, contact, address, and city.
If the table does not exist, create it.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Explanation
This requirement focuses on excluding employees with a specific name.
Each employee has a name column.
The condition checks whether the name is not equal to 'Amit'.
Only employees whose name is different from 'Amit' are included.
Employees named Amit are excluded from the result.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------

root

create database employee;

use employee;

create table employee(id int primary key , name varchar(50), salary decimal(10,2), email varchar(100), contact varchar(150), address varchar(150),city varchar(50));

desc employee;

insert into employee value(1, 'Rahul', 60000, 'rahul@email.com', '9876543210', '123 Street, Pune', 'Pune'),(2, 'Amit', 55000, 'amit@email.com', '9876501234', 'Mumbai Road, Mumbai', 'Mumbai'),(3, 'Sneha', 70000, 'sneha@email.com', '9123456789', 'MG Road, Bangalore', 'Bangalore'),(4, 'Priya', 65000, 'priya@email.com', '9988776655', 'Delhi Street, Delhi', 'Delhi'),(5, 'Ramesh', 80000, 'ramesh@email.com', '9123456780', '456 Avenue, Pune', 'Pune'),(7, 'sahil', 40000, 'sahil@gmail.com', '9876543211', 'Andheri', 'Mumbai'), (8, 'Rohit', 55000, 'rohit@gmail.com', null , 'Baner', 'Pune');

